      "generator": "Codex 内置 ImageGen",
      "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story for an original first-grade Chinese interactive reading lesson. Produce one flat rectangular atlas of exactly 3 columns x 2 rows of equal square panels, all six have different simple illustrated scenes. Grid boundaries are at thirds of width and half of height, no gutter, each is independently full bleed and self-contained; no object crosses a cell edge, key subjects stay away from every edge. No words, letters, numbers, punctuation, arrows, printed marks or watermark anywhere. Same warm tactile storybook art in every panel: fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut paper shapes, pine green and warm cream, muted rain blue and apricot and persimmon orange accents, calm background, large clear shapes visible at thumbnail size. Not photoreal or 3D.\nTOP LEFT: cloud radio booth on a fluffy open cloud beneath a quiet rainy blue sky. One simple wooden microphone on a small desk near two charming expressive anthropomorphic raindrop characters. The large slate-blue teardrop wears a short orange scarf, the smaller turquoise teardrop wears a small dark green leaf cap; the large body is about 1.7 times the size of the small body. Both are easy to tell apart, no other faces in the rain. See both full bodies, room at edges.\nTOP MIDDLE: a child with orange scarf and pale teal jacket sits under a porch, points with one finger to one of THREE separate small paper lanterns on a simple cream cloth as the child counts them. Show whole three lanterns in a spaced horizontal row, other hand can show tally fingers. The child's face and counting finger are clearly visible. No other objects competing with the lanterns, not a marketplace.\nTOP RIGHT: the same child kneels close and carefully watches exactly ONE little pale green leaf pushing up on a short stem in a small terracotta pot of dark soil. Place plant in open space in middle, not an image of a mature plant, show only one pot. No diagram lines.\nBOTTOM LEFT: the same child holds both empty hands up, brows and head tilted in a clearly inquisitive, politely asking expression, facing a friend with a pine-green vest at a simple porch rail. Friend is listening quietly, eyes toward questioner, friendly. Show both faces and open hands with lots of empty margin. No speech bubbles or lettering.\nBOTTOM MIDDLE: same two children and porch but the friend now answers and clearly points sideways toward a small lantern on a stool. First child now listens with hands down, clear turn-taking and unmistakable contrast with panel at bottom left. No lettering or speech bubbles.\nBOTTOM RIGHT: a tiny cream and dark pine-green toy boat with apricot prow in a quiet outdoor rain puddle, a round clear soap bubble floating above the prow and small puddle rings, beside a painted tabletop sign with a simple yellow paper lantern pictured but no text. Balanced miniature playful scene, no frame and no interface.\nEach panel must stay fully visible after cropping inside the outer 4% edge. The artwork is original, no reference to published textbook composition."
    },
