      "generator": "Codex 内置 ImageGen",
      "prompt": "Use case: isolated sprite assets for an original first-grade Chinese story game, one true transparent PNG atlas. Produce exactly 3 by 3 grid of equal square cells, nine separate illustrations with only transparent pixel gaps, no background or labels. Boundaries at thirds. Each sprite remains centered in its cell with clear completely transparent margins. No text, arrows, letters, words, numerals or watermark. All same approved tactile style: fine paper grain, matte gouache, clean cut-paper contours, deep pine green, warm cream, muted rain blue and persimmon-orange accents. Strong readable silhouette at 32 pixels, no particle trails beyond the bounds. No grid lines.\nROW ONE LEFT: anthropomorphic slate-blue teardrop with small apricot orange scarf, large rounded bottom and pointed head. Two tiny arms, two tiny dark blue shoes and a warm simple face. Clearly visible large body. CENTER: a matching smaller rounded turquoise teardrop character with a small pine-green leaf hat, a tiny face and two dark blue shoes, body about 60 percent the height of left sprite. RIGHT: one dark pine-green vintage toy delivery car in side view with light cream open cargo bed, two dark wheels, orange tip facing RIGHT.\nROW TWO LEFT: same car in the exact same view and silhouette, now softly glowing at its orange nose as a second action frame. CENTER: one tiny flat cream and dark pine-green toy boat in side view with apricot prow pointing RIGHT and a simple pale paper sail. No water, shadow or bubbles. RIGHT: the exact same boat in the exact same position and view with one small translucent bubble at prow as the second animation frame, the boat still fills most of this cell.\nROW THREE LEFT: exactly one simple upward-facing red five-petal wildflower atop one straight thin green stem and two green leaves, no pot, bare stem visible all the way to its bottom; petal shape is unmistakably red. CENTER: one isolated compact bright grass tuft of five green long narrow blades, clearly pointed up, no ground or soil beneath it. RIGHT: one small original vintage table microphone with amber grille, pine green stand, warm cream accent. Single mic, no wire or shadow.\nFinish all outlines and margins clearly. Keep the actual background fully transparent, no fake checkerboards or off-white."
